<meta type=article>
<title | Shorthand catalog>
</meta>

Every authoring shorthand — the sigil cipher and each element’s alias / expansion forms — with what it compiles to in Layer 1, generated from the vocabulary source so the shorthand→Layer 1 mapping is inherent and can’t drift. The canonical elements these compile to are documented in the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog" | Layer 1 catalog>.

<section #sh-sigils | Sigil forms>

The tagname↔sigil cipher — the fewest-keystrokes form for sections, math, and code.

<section #sh-sigil-section | `<# … #>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<section>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-section" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <section>.*

<code>
<# Methods #>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<# Methods #>
</frame>

<section #sh-sigil-sub-section | `<## … ##>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<sub-section>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-sub-section" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <sub-section>.*

<code>
<## Materials ##>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<## Materials ##>
</frame>

<section #sh-sigil-sub-sub-section | `<### … ###>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<sub-sub-section>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-sub-sub-section" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <sub-sub-section>.*

<code>
<### Reagents ###>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<### Reagents ###>
</frame>

<section #sh-sigil-inline-math | `<$ … $>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<inline-math>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-inline-math" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <inline-math>.*

<code>
Euler: <$ e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0 $>.
</code>

<frame -numbered>
Euler: <$ e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0 $>.
</frame>

<section #sh-sigil-display-math | `<$$ … $$>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<display-math>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-display-math" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <display-math>.*

<code>
<$$ \int_0^1 x^2 \, dx = \tfrac{1}{3} $$>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<$$ \int_0^1 x^2 \, dx = \tfrac{1}{3} $$>
</frame>

<section #sh-sigil-inline-code | `<` … `>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<inline-code>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-inline-code" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <inline-code>.*

<code>
Call <` build() `> to start.
</code>

<frame -numbered>
Call <` build() `> to start.
</frame>

<section #sh-sigil-code-block | `<``` … ```>`>

Expands to the Layer 1 `<code-block>` (see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-code-block" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The sigil shorthand for <code-block>.*

<code>
<``` js
const x = 1;
```>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<``` js
const x = 1;
```>
</frame>

<section #sh-aliases | Tag aliases>

Alternate authoring names that normalize to a canonical element.

<section #sh-exp-quote | `<quote>`>

Expands to `<blockquote>` (the Layer 1 `<blockquote>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-blockquote" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Authoring shortcut. <quote> is the preferred authoring form; <blockquote> is the Layer 1 element. The shorthand expands at the interpreter; the rendered HTML uses HTML's native <blockquote>.*

<code>
<quote type=epigraph |
All happy families are alike; each unhappy family is unhappy in its own way.
>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<quote type=epigraph |
All happy families are alike; each unhappy family is unhappy in its own way.
>
</frame>

<section #sh-exp-figure | `<figure>`>

Expands to `<fig>` (the Layer 1 `<fig>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-fig" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*`<figure>` is an accepted authoring alias for the canonical `<fig>`, recorded in `DESIGN.md` §"Frameable elements: a shared capability". The normalize-to-canonical gate rewrites `<figure>`-authored node tagnames to `fig` before downstream plugins run, so the entire pipeline below the gate sees the canonical name. Both shorthand_expansions (this vocab-level alias) and the gate rewrite exist together because they serve different needs: the vocab alias makes `<figure>` survive a bypass of the gate (defensive), and the gate rewrite ensures tagname-keyed downstream lookups (NUMBERED_TAGNAMES, handler routing) see the single canonical name.*

<code>
<figure src=elephant.jpg | An adult African elephant.>
</code>

<frame -numbered>
<figure -numbered src=elephant.jpg | An adult African elephant.>
</frame>

*`<figure>` is the authoring alias. The normalize-to-canonical gate rewrites the tagname to `fig` early; the rendered output is the same.*

<section #sh-expansions | Expansion shorthands>

Shorthand tags that expand to a Layer 1 element with attributes set (e.g. the book-part family).

<section #sh-exp-chapter | `<chapter>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="chapter">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*The most common book-part type.*

<code>
<chapter | Origins>
Content of the chapter.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the live examples and the demo book.*

<section #sh-exp-part | `<part>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="part">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Named major divisions ("Part I: Foundations").*

<code>
<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Chapter>
Content.

<chapter | Second Chapter>
Content.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the live examples and the demo book.*

<section #sh-exp-appendix | `<appendix>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="appendix">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Typically appears in book-back.*

<section #sh-exp-preface | `<preface>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="preface">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Front-matter prose by the author. Typically in book-front.*

<code>
<preface | A Note from the Author>
I wrote this book because...

<chapter | Chapter One>
Body content.

<appendix | Notation>
Notation conventions used in this book.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the live examples and the demo book.*

*The structural plugin places the preface in book-front, the chapter in book-body, and the appendix in book-back based on book-part-type.*

<section #sh-exp-foreword | `<foreword>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="foreword">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Front-matter prose by someone other than the author.*

<section #sh-exp-introduction | `<introduction>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="introduction">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

<section #sh-exp-conclusion | `<conclusion>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="conclusion">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

<section #sh-exp-glossary | `<glossary>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="glossary">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

<section #sh-exp-dedication | `<dedication>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="dedication">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Front-matter dedication. Typically in book-front.*

<section #sh-exp-afterword | `<afterword>`>

Expands to `<book-part type="afterword">` (the Layer 1 `<book-part>`, see the <a href="?page=layer-1-catalog#l1-book-part" | Layer 1 catalog>).

*Back-matter closing prose. Typically in book-back.*

